An arithmetization of an arbitrary CCC would still require a computable assignment
of objects and arrows to an arithmetic backend, a stated and proved equality notion,
faithfulness, preservation of terminal objects, products, and exponentials, and
honest resource bounds for composition, evaluation, curry, and equality checking.
The present development supplies exact pieces of that map and rules out the naive
fixed finite-table version.  It does not pretend the remaining engineering and
cryptographic obligations are already discharged.
